    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d434">

                <pb facs="0628" n="514" sameAs="frus:frus1922v02/pg514"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">838.51/1374: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The High Commissioner in Haiti</hi> (<hi
                        rendition="#italic">Russell</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Acting
                        Secretary of State</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Port au Prince</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1922-09-15T12:00:00-05:00"><hi rendition="#italic">September 15,
                                1922—noon</hi></date>.<lb/>[Received September 16—10:05
                        a.m.]</dateline></opener>
                <p>106. In reply to my note containing the suggestions made by the Department’s 73,
                    September 9, 4 p.m. the Haitian Government informs me that it has taken note of
                    suggestions and will place them before the legislative committee now examining
                    the proposed law.<anchor n="62" xml:id="d434-f1"/></p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Russell</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d434-f1" n="62" xml:id="d434-f1-content">
                <p>The law, embodying the Department’s suggestions, was passed by the Council of
                    State Sept. 27, approved by President Borno Oct. 2, and published in <hi
                        rendition="#italic">Le Moniteur</hi> Oct. 5, 1922.</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
    </standOff>
